Create EC2 instance through terraform
---------------------------------------------------------
Terraform file extension is .tf
provider.tf -> where you can declare what provider you are using like AWS, Azure, GCP and so on
search in google like terraform provider, here can see all providers like azure, aws, gcp and so on, click on AWS click on providers right side top and below you can see some code copy and paste in VS code.

Create Terrafrom folder in VS code, under Terrafrom create EC2 folder and under EC2 create a file provider.tf
terraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "6.27.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  # Configuration options         ==> here u have to give authentication information -> if i give authentication info here and if i push to github secret key and credentials will be public
}
copy and paste above content in provider.tf file

